@startuml Sequence Diagram - CIM Data Import
!theme vibrant
title Sequence Diagram - CIM Data Import & Transformation

actor "Engineer" as User
participant "Frontend" as Frontend
participant "CimController" as Controller
participant "CimTransformerService" as Transformer
participant "JenaService" as Jena
participant "OntModel\n(OWL Reasoner)" as OntModel
database "Knowledge Graph\n(TDB2)" as KG

User -> Frontend: Upload CIM file\n(XML/RDF format)

Frontend -> Controller: POST /api/cim/import\nMultipartFile
activate Controller

Controller -> Controller: Validate file:\n- Size < 100MB\n- Format supported\n- Not empty

alt File validation fails
  Controller --> Frontend: HTTP 400 Bad Request
  Frontend --> User: "Invalid file"
else File validation OK

  == Step 1: Parse & Transform ==
  Controller -> Transformer: transformCimXmlToRdf(\ninputStream)
  activate Transformer

  Transformer -> Transformer: Parse CIM/XML
  note right
    Parse CIM elements:
    - Substations
    - Transmission Lines
    - Generators
    - Transformers
    - Breakers
    - Connectivity Nodes
  end note

  Transformer -> Transformer: Map to RDF/OWL
  note right
    Transform to triples:

    <Substation_123>
      rdf:type cim:Substation
      cim:name "Main Station"
      cim:voltage "110000"
      cim:location "..."
  end note

  Transformer --> Controller: RDF Model\n(in-memory)
  deactivate Transformer

  == Step 2: Validate Schema ==
  Controller -> Transformer: validateCimSchema(model)
  activate Transformer

  Transformer -> OntModel: Check ontology compliance
  activate OntModel

  OntModel -> OntModel: Verify:\n- Class definitions\n- Property domains/ranges\n- Cardinality constraints

  alt Schema validation fails
    OntModel --> Transformer: Validation errors
    deactivate OntModel
    Transformer --> Controller: ValidationResult\n{valid: false, errors: [...]}
    deactivate Transformer
    Controller --> Frontend: HTTP 422 Unprocessable
    Frontend --> User: Show validation errors
  else Schema validation OK
    OntModel --> Transformer: Valid
    deactivate OntModel
    Transformer --> Controller: ValidationResult\n{valid: true}
    deactivate Transformer

    == Step 3: Enrich with Inference ==
    Controller -> Transformer: enrichWithInferences(model)
    activate Transformer

    Transformer -> OntModel: Apply OWL reasoning
    activate OntModel

    OntModel -> OntModel: Infer new triples:\n- Transitive properties\n- Inverse properties\n- Class hierarchies
    note right
      Example inferred triples:

      If: Line_456 connects Sub_A to Sub_B
      Infer: Sub_A is connected to Sub_B
             (inverse relationship)

      If: Transformer_789 is in Sub_A
          Sub_A powers Region_North
      Infer: Transformer_789 indirectly
             powers Region_North
    end note

    OntModel --> Transformer: Enriched model
    deactivate OntModel
    Transformer --> Controller: Enriched RDF Model
    deactivate Transformer

    == Step 4: Import to Knowledge Graph ==
    Controller -> Jena: importRdfData(\nmodel, "RDF/XML")
    activate Jena

    Jena -> KG: Begin transaction
    activate KG

    Jena -> KG: Write triples to TDB2
    note right
      Persistent storage of:
      - Original triples
      - Inferred triples
      - Metadata
    end note

    KG --> Jena: Transaction committed
    deactivate KG

    Jena -> Jena: Update statistics
    Jena --> Controller: Import successful\n{triplesCount: 15743}
    deactivate Jena

    == Step 5: Generate Statistics ==
    Controller -> Jena: getGraphStatistics()
    activate Jena

    Jena -> KG: Query statistics
    activate KG
    KG --> Jena: Stats data
    deactivate KG

    Jena --> Controller: {\n totalTriples,\n totalSubjects,\n totalClasses,\n ...\n}
    deactivate Jena

    Controller --> Frontend: HTTP 200 OK\n{\n status: "success",\n triplesImported: 15743,\n inferredTriples: 3421,\n statistics: {...}\n}
    deactivate Controller

    Frontend -> Frontend: Show success message\n+ statistics
    Frontend --> User: "Import successful!\n15,743 triples imported"

  end
end

== Post-Import Operations ==
User -> Frontend: View imported data
Frontend -> Controller: GET /api/cim/statistics
activate Controller
Controller -> Jena: getGraphStatistics()
activate Jena
Jena --> Controller: Statistics
deactivate Jena
Controller --> Frontend: Statistics JSON
deactivate Controller
Frontend --> User: Display dashboard

note over User, KG
  **Performance:**
  - Small file (< 1MB): 1-2 seconds
  - Medium file (10MB): 5-10 seconds
  - Large file (100MB): 30-60 seconds

  **Statistics tracked:**
  - Total triples
  - Equipment count by type
  - Network connectivity
  - Inference coverage
end note

@enduml
